 strategies, such as the ketogenic diet, where fasting may enhance its effectiveness. Prolonged fasting, whether pre-operative or post-operative, may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to maintain adequate nutrient intake. Furthermore, fasting is recognized as a physiological factor that can influence energy expenditure, especially in pediatric patients, and it is known to stimulate the secretion of growth hormone. Overall, AYUNO encompasses a range of medical and dietary implications, highlighting its significance in both clinical and nutritional contexts.", "ESTRÉS METABÓLICO:El estrés metabólico puede afectar la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar nutrientes, lo que puede hacer necesaria la nutrición parenteral.", "RECHAZO DE INTERVENCIÓN:El rechazo de la intervención por parte del paciente o su representante legal puede influir en la decisión de administrar nutrición parenteral.", "EMULSIONES LIPÍDICAS:Emulsiones lipídicas are lipid emulsions utilized in parenteral nutrition to deliver essential fatty acids and calories, thereby preventing complications that may arise from glucose-only nutrition. These emulsions serve as energy substrates without increasing osmolarity, making them suitable for incorporation into parenteral nutrition regimens. Composed of triglycerides, oils, and emulsifiers, emulsiones lipídicas provide a vital source of energy and essential fatty acids for patients. Their varying compositions can lead to different effects on patients, highlighting the importance of tailored nutritional support in clinical settings.", "TRIGLICÉRIDOS DE CADENA LARGA:TRIGLICÉRIDOS DE CADENA LARGA, or long-chain triglycerides, are a type of fat that plays a significant role in early lipid emulsions used for parenteral nutrition. These triglycerides are derived from soybean oil and are rich in essential fatty acids, making them an important source of nutrition in medical settings.", "ÁCIDOS GRASOS ESENCIALES:Ácidos Grasos Esenciales are vital nutrients that the body cannot synthesize on its own, necessitating their acquisition through diet or supplementation. These essential fatty acids, such as linoleic acid and alpha-linolenic acid, play a crucial role in various bodily functions, including modulating inflammatory responses and improving health outcomes, particularly for individuals with conditions like cystic fibrosis. Their importance in maintaining overall health underscores the need for adequate dietary intake of these necessary fats.", "ÁCIDO LINOLÉICO:El ácido linoleico es un ácido graso esencial que debe ser aportado en la dieta y es importante para la salud metabólica.", "ÁCIDO ALFA-LINOLÉNICO:El ácido alfa-linolénico es un ácido graso omega-3 esencial que debe ser incluido en la dieta para mantener la salud.", "ALFA TOCOFEROL:Alfa tocopherol is a form of Vitamin E that serves as an important antioxidant. It is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition and is also found in lipid emulsions, where it plays a crucial role in preventing peroxidation. This compound is essential for maintaining cellular health and protecting against oxidative stress.", "PANCREATITIS:Pancreatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can lead to severe abdominal pain, digestive issues, and nutritional deficiencies. This inflammation can significantly affect digestion, often necessitating enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutritional support for patients. In pediatric patients, pancreatitis can notably increase energy expenditure, presenting additional metabolic challenges. The condition can be acute or chronic and may require medical intervention due to its potential complications, including malnutrition and the need for specialized treatment.\n\nFurthermore, pancreatitis can arise as a serious complication in patients with severe metabolic disorders and has been reported in individuals following a ketogenic diet. It is important to exercise caution in drug use for patients with this condition, as it can lead to further complications. In certain cases, the use of lipid emulsions may be indicated to support nutritional needs. Overall, pancreatitis is a severe condition that demands careful management and monitoring by healthcare professionals.", "ACEITE DE SOJA:El \"ACEITE DE SOJA\" es un aceite que se deriva de las semillas de soja y se caracteriza por ser una fuente de triglicéridos de cadena larga, lo que lo hace útil en emulsiones lipídicas. Además, el aceite de soja es rico en ácidos grasos esenciales, lo que lo convierte en un componente recomendado en la dieta de personas que padecen trastornos de la β-oxidación. Sin embargo, en el contexto de la nutrición en cuidados críticos, se menciona que el aceite de soja, como fuente de ácidos grasos omega-6, debería ser reducido. A pesar de esta recomendación, el aceite de soja sigue siendo utilizado como fuente de lípidos en la nutrición parenteral.", "ACEITE DE COCO:El \"ACEITE DE COCO\" es un tipo de grasa que se caracteriza por su contenido en triglicéridos de cadena media (TCM), los cuales se metabolizan rápidamente y son utilizados en emulsiones lipídicas. Este aceite contiene proporciones significativas de ácidos grasos saturados de cadena media, que tienen un efecto diferente en el organismo en comparación con los ácidos grasos de cadena larga. Además, el aceite de coco puede ser beneficioso en la dieta de personas que padecen trastornos de la β-oxidación, ya que su composición permite una utilización más eficiente de los lípidos.", "LECITINA DE HUEVO:La lecitina de huevo es un emulgente utilizado para estabilizar emulsiones lipídicas.", "GLICEROL:Glicerol, also known as glycerin, is a three-carbon molecule that plays a significant role in various biological and chemical processes. It is commonly used as an isotonizing agent in the formulation of lipid emulsions, where it helps maintain the appropriate osmolarity. Additionally, glicerol can be converted into glucose through the process of gluconeogenesis, highlighting its importance in energy metabolism."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}